{
 "_source": "https://fruitychutes.com/parachuteapi.js?method=get&term=<SKU> (the data API behind Fruity Chutes own descent-rate calculator), fetched 2026-09-03. SKU list: method=list&term=IFC|CFC|TARC&page=0.",
 "_why": "Owner ruling 2026-09-03 (issues-2026-09-03b): “For Fruity Chutes, the standing rule should be to take the information they have on their website as canonical and it should supercede anything from other sources.”",
 "_cdConvention": "dragCoefficient is their cd_projected, referenced to the canopy area MINUS the spill hole. Our kernel uses the nominal diameter with cd_eff = cd*(1-(d/D)^2), which is algebraically the same area - so Cd and spill hole MUST be applied together or the descent rate is wrong. Verified: their published “lb @ 20 fps” rating reproduces from cd_projected * area_projected on all 68 models, to 0.5%.",
 "_spillRatios": "Their own constants: 0.176*D for every Iris, 0.20*D for every Classic and TARC. NOTE the TARC family page instead states a 10% AREA spill hole (5 / 5.7 / 6.3 / 7.6 in), which is 0.316*D and contradicts this API. The API pair is used because Cd and spill must come from the same source; flagged for the owner.",
 "_lineLength": "Fruity Chutes publish shroud-line LENGTH only for TARC (family-page table, carried here as lineLengthM). For every other model the merge script keeps whatever length the existing catalogue row has, or derives it from a sibling - it is a convention, never presented as Fruity Chutes data.",
 "_fetched": "2026-09-03",
